bodyHtml: |
  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>According to the Bormes-les-Mimosas town hall, Le Gouron beach lies between La Favière and Le Lavandou, at the eastern end of the town's coastline.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the official website of the Bormes-les-Mimosas town hall (page updated 13 March 2025), which restricts dogs to a few specific areas from 15 June to 30 September, Le Gouron beach is one of the only two exceptions allowed in high season, along with the small <a href="/en/fiche-bormes-les-mimosas">Fort de Brégançon beach</a> at the other end of the town. Dogs must be kept on a leash and their waste picked up. Outside that period, the town hall mentions no other restriction. Only assistance dogs are allowed on the rest of the municipal beaches.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: handy if you arrive via Le Lavandou and want a proper beach with your dog without waiting for sunset — Le Gouron is within easy reach as soon as you cross the town boundary.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>La Favière harbour and the centre of Bormes-les-Mimosas are a few minutes away. Le Lavandou, just beyond, has its own rules: check before you go.</p>
